1.1.evidence:
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE MAYOR OF TUAL,

Considering : a. that as citizens, women and children have the right to obtain protection from any acts of violence committed against them that cause physical or psychological harm, as part of the recognition and enforcement of human rights;
b. that protection for women and children victims of violence is an effort to provide a sense of security and freedom from all acts of violence guaranteed by Pancasila as the state philosophy, the Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia as the highest legal basis in the state as well as various other laws and regulations;
c. that protection for women and children victims of violence is one aspect of the duties and responsibilities of regional government in providing protection and services to the community;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish by Regional Regulation of Tual City concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 60 of 1958 concerning the Stipulation of Law Number 23 of 1957 concerning the Establishment of Level II Autonomous Regions Within the Level I Autonomous Region of Maluku (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1958 Number 111, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1645);
